# Techtrick CMS — example configuration.
# Copy to .env and adjust. .env is git-ignored; never commit real secrets.

# --- Runtime (read by the container at start) --------------------------------
# Port the SSR server listens on inside the container.
PORT=3000
# Bind address. Keep 0.0.0.0 so Docker can map the port.
HOST=0.0.0.0
# Always "production" for a self-hosted deployment.
NODE_ENV=production

# --- Build-time --------------------------------------------------------------
# Nitro output target. The Dockerfile sets this to node-server so the build
# emits .output/server/index.mjs instead of the default Cloudflare worker.
# Only override if you deploy somewhere else.
NITRO_PRESET=node-server

# --- Application ---------------------------------------------------------------
# No application secrets are required today: the app ships with mock data from
# src/data/cms-mock.ts and has no backend.
#
# When you wire up a real data source, anything the browser must read has to be
# prefixed with VITE_ (it is inlined into the client bundle at build time — do
# not put secrets there). Server-only values stay unprefixed and are read from
# process.env inside server code.
# VITE_APP_NAME=Techtrick CMS
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/techtrick
